# YAGNI — build only what was asked

Implement only what the current request requires. Do not add features, endpoints, config, or infrastructure for hypothetical future needs.

## Default

- **Requested scope only** — if the user didn't ask for it, don't build it.
- **Note, don't build** — if a future need is obvious, mention it in one line; do not implement it.
- **No feature creep** — common extras (auth flows, admin UIs, plugin systems, watch modes) require explicit request.
- **Foresight ≠ speculation** — design so future changes are possible; don't build them now.

## Agent bias to resist

Agents reproduce mature codebases. A "simple converter" does not need plugins, config files, or live reload unless requested.

## When extras are allowed

- User explicitly asks
- Security, accessibility, or compliance the task genuinely requires
- Bug fix needs a minimal adjacent change to be correct

## Example constraint

"Build X only. Do not add Y or Z — we can add those later if needed."
